CIADDYFILE EXAMPLE FOR WIREGUARD WITH AUTH
===========================================

Place this as /etc/caddy/Caddyfile (or wherever Caddy config lives):

# Replace with your actual domain/public IP
yuhanbae.vpn.io {
    # HTTP BASIC auth using dynamically generated users.json
    # See generate-auth.py to create users.json from the credentials
    basicauth users.json wg-auth.json

    # Reverse proxy to WireGuard host (if running on same machine)
    # Or point to your WireGuard server's IP:port
    reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:51820

    # Optional: Log format
    log {
        output file /var/log/caddy/wg-access.log
        format json
    }
}

# To generate wg-auth.json from credentials:
#   python3 generate-auth.py 198305052005011001 3ntahlaH
# This creates users.json with hashed password for Caddy BASIC auth

# To generate users.json:
#   echo '{"198305052005011001": "$6$...hash..."}' > users.json
#   The hash can be generated with: pip install passlib && python3 -c "from passlib.hash import bcrypt; print(bcrypt.hash('3ntahlaH'))"